Spec: Terminal Confirmation Prompt

Purpose:
  Obtain an explicit default-No confirmation from an interactive terminal.

Owns:
  ./confirmation-prompt.ts
  ./confirmation-prompt.test.ts

References:
  ../constants.sdd

Must:
  Accept injectable input and output streams, defaulting to standard input and standard output.
  Return `false` without reading input unless both streams are interactive terminals.
  Display `Continue? [y/N] ` and accept only trimmed, case-insensitive `y` or `yes`.
  Return `false` for all other answers, EOF, interruption, or stream failure.
  Release the readline interface and event handlers after every outcome.

Exposes:
  @ConfirmationPrompt
  @ConfirmationPrompt.confirm
